<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:orl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Logging;assembly=OpenRigs.Logging"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>What the device pieces read from an experiment, for a workflow that makes no experiment folder (a calibration, a preflight), in place of LaunchSettings and ExperimentLogs: PathPrefix, declared and never published, so no piece's log starts and nothing is written under rig.yml's rootPath; Events, declared and never written, for the events a piece sends (LickSpoutStage's spout positions); and SubjectId from Start, the property SubjectId: _no-experiment_, one name for every such workflow and no mouse's, so LickSpoutStage's in positions are rig.yml's lickSpoutDefaultPosition. Included once, with neither ExperimentLogs nor LaunchSettings, and the workflow declares neither subject itself (no_experiment_folder_problems).</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="SubjectId" Description="The subject the pieces see: _no-experiment_, no mouse's, so no mouse's spout positions are read or saved. A launch may set a mouse's." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
          <Value>_no-experiment_</Value>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
          <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
        <Name>SubjectId</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:String">
        <rx:Name>PathPrefix</rx:Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="harp:Timestamped(orl:EventRow)">
        <rx:Name>Events</rx:Name>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
